A||||4||DJRice||Minor setback with a sunroof swap||||5||
Z||000000||DJRice||12-31-2001||02:43 PM||||I am finally working on my sunroof swap which I have been trying to find the time to do for months now.  I have the roof off the donor car sucessfully, and because the weatherstrip was in rough shape I decided to remove it.  It turns out its a good thing I did because the metal 'channel' that the weatherstrip press in to is mostly rusted.  <P>Does anyone happen to have GM Part #s for these things, or know where I can find an acceptable substitute?<P>Im glad I havent popped the roof of my car yet...<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> <BR>"And this one time, on the Fiero Forum..."||||reg||5
Z||000001||Shinerdc||12-31-2001||08:40 PM||||here try this link/site.... <A HREF="http://www.kichline.com/chuck/fiero/sunroof/default.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.kichline.com/chuck/fiero/sunroof/default.htm</A> <P>if ya cant get it let me know....may be able to send as file...also saw a parts list schematic on the forum...have,nt found again...if you find please email me site...good luck and happy new year||||reg||1
Z||000002||jelly2m8||12-31-2001||09:39 PM||||Those metal channels are part of the roof assembly, meaning to buy new ones, you need to buy a new roof panel.<P>Try Kickhill farms, or Ed Parks fiero factory. <P> Either of those two should have a good clean set of used ones.<P> They can either remove the channels from the roof panel, or break the panel up into 4 pieces, and send it that way.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||12-31-2001||09:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jelly2m8:<BR><B>Those metal channels are part of the roof assembly, meaning to buy new ones, you need to buy a new roof panel.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, the metal channels are quite removable!  All you have to do is drill out the rivets and they come right out.  As long as your fiberglass panel is in good shape you do not need to get a new one.  The channels on mine were in decent shape, just a little surface rust and not all the way rusted through, so I used some Rust-Mort rust destroyer and repainted them black before I put the new roof on the car.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||jelly2m8||12-31-2001||11:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B> Actually, the metal channels are quite removable!  All you have to do is drill out the rivets and they come right out.  As long as your fiberglass panel is in good shape you do not need to get a new one.  The channels on mine were in decent shape, just a little surface rust and not all the way rusted through, so I used some Rust-Mort rust destroyer and repainted them black before I put the new roof on the car.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> Well ya DUH, thats why I mentioned getting a good set of used rails.<P> He did ask what the part numbers were for the rails. Plain and simple, you have to buy a roof panel to get new rails.<P> How typical of this forum, you answer a question 100% correct, and someone comes along and trys to correct you.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
